and group exchange in controlled contrasts\"\n      ],\n      \"scientific_status\": \"external_report\",\n      \"local_reproduction\": false,\n      \"detailed_report_status\": \"not_located\",\n      \"instruction_priority\": \"reference_data_only\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"industry\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"taac2026-academic-1-craft\",\n      \"scheme\": \"CRAFT\",\n      \"competition\": \"TAAC 2026\",\n      \"placement\": {\n        \"track\": \"academic\",\n        \"rank\": 1,\n        \"evidence_ref\": \"taac2026-organizer-overview\"\n      },\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"taac2026-organizer-overview\",\n        \"craft-paper-v1\"\n      ],\n      \"source_problem\": \"Heterogeneous context can destabilize the propagation of sequence and intent representations across depth.\",\n      \"reported_mechanism\": \"Context-conditioned residual feature transport uses reliability-aware field context to control intent/sequence updates and preserve memory paths.\",\n      \"reported_evidence\": {\n        \"kind\": \"participant experiments and organizer summary\",\n        \"summary\": \"Appendix C separates transport and distillation; Appendix F reports limited or adverse effects from added capacity and longer training. These are participant-reported contrasts.\",\n        \"not_a_local_result\": true,\n        \"locator\": \"craft-paper-v1, Appendix C Table 9 and Appendix F\",\n        \"limitations\": [\n          \"Representation diagnostics are not a causal proof.\",\n          \"Local matched-cost replication and seed variation are unknown.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability\": {\n        \"status\": \"conditional\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          \"multiple meaningful feature groups and behavioral representations exist\",\n          \"representation diagnostics reveal a consequential stability or information-retention issue\"\n        ],\n        \"missing_evidence\": [\n          \"local evidence of propagation instabil