{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The source review sharpens the question: DIN already discusses both pooling and preserving interest intensity, so this is a local attribution study without a novelty claim. I’ve implemented uniform pooling and learned weighting that omits the target query, each with a matched activity-only control.\n\nThe models retain the parent’s allocated parameters and initialization order. Uniform pooling skips the scoring network, leaving those parameters unused; any speed benefit remains to be measured."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\npath = Path('/workspace/candidate.py')\nsource = path.read_text()\ntree = ast.parse(source)\nconfig_node = next(n for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t, ast.Name) and t.id == 'CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\nbase_config = ast.literal_eval(config_node.value)\nvariants = []\nsettings = [\n    ('mean_match', 'candidate.py', 'candidate', 'mean', 'match'),\n    ('mean_activity', 'mean_activity.py', 'control', 'mean', 'activity'),\n    ('content_match', 'content_match.py', 'candidate', 'content', 'match'),\n    ('content_activity', 'content_activity.py', 'control', 'content', 'activity'),\n]\nfor name, filename, role, mode, relevance in settings:\n    config = dict(base_config, summary_mode=mode, relevance_mode=relevance)\n    if filename \"'!= '\"'candidate.py':\n        lines = source.splitlines(keepends=True)\n        replacement = 'CONFIG = ' + repr(config) + '\\\\n'\n        lines[config_node.lineno - 1:config_node.end_lineno] = [replacement]\n        Path('/workspace', filename).write_text(''.join(lines))\n    variants.append({\n        'name': name, 'file': filename, 'role': role, 'config': config,\n        'note': (\n            ('Uniform masked mean of the unchanged trainable event values; bypass the scorer. '\n             if mode == 'mean' else\n             'Keep the exact parent scoring network but replace its target query by zeros: score [0,h,-h,0]. ')\n            + ('Retain all four bounded log-count slots N,C,B,J. ' if relevance == 'match' else\n               'Preserve N exactly, zero the C/B/J slots; same output width and allocations. ')\n            + 'Train from scratch with frozen host protocol and seed 42. No custom optimizer or loss. '\n              'Allocated parameter tensors and initialization order match g1-r0002-joint_count; effective capacity differs. '\n              'Standalone numeric-only module. Syntax and structural checks are local; Torch execution is unavailable. '\n              'Compare against existing g1-r0002-joint_count and g1-r0003-attention_activity for the corresponding target-aware cells.'\n        )\n    })\n\nfixed = [\n    'Protocol 9c1635366a72f4c4f67708ee7ae9b72a1b90197ffed3485736388ceff7c91d3e; supplied causal history, mask and length limit 128',\n    'Static fields, bucket embeddings and additive category/brand/action/log-age event values, embedding width 16',\n    'Allocated parameter tensors and creation order; hidden widths [128,64]; four statistic input columns',\n    'log1p counts / log(129), observed J, zero/missing IDs excluded from matches',\n    'Host scratch training, three full data passes, natural labels, batch 4096, Adam with lr .001, seed 42, checkpoint selection and scorers',\n]\nconfounds = [\n    'Active capacity is not matched: mean mode leaves all 4226 scorer parameters dormant; content mode has zero query/product columns and redundant h/-h inputs. Allocated capacity is matched.',\n    'Training-mediated representation norms and embedding gradients change; a gap alone cannot distinguish useful information from optimization or scale effects.',\n    'Existing attention controls were executed earlier; host timing variation and single seed can affect comparisons. Use only paired final validation seeds before a repeated-support claim.',\n]\ncontrast_specs = [\n    ('g1-r0002-joint_count',\n     'mean_match replaces target-aware event weights by mask/N while retaining N,C,B,J; content_match separately zeros only the scorer query.',\n     'Existing target-aware attention with N,C,B,J: g1-r0002-joint_count.',\n     'If mean_match meets the screening quality tolerance and improves measured cost, advance it as the simpler candidate. If only content_match preserves quality, learned event weighting may matter while direct query injection may be dispensable.',\n     'If both replacements lose more than .0003 AUC or .0001 Logloss, keep the incumbent and retain evidence of conditional value in this target-aware implementation. Do not refute all pooling from a single implementation.'),\n    ('g1-r0003-attention_activity',\n     'mean_activity and content_activity replace history weighting with the same interventions but retain only N and zero all target-match slots.',\n     'Existing target-aware attention plus N-only readout: g1-r0003-attention_activity.',\n     'Compare AUC_target_aware - AUC_replacement in the match and activity conditions. A smaller gap with matches (difference at least .0003 for screening) supports partial substitution by direct relevance; assess each replacement separately.',\n     'If query/weighting gaps do not shrink with matches, reject the partial-substitution prediction even if a cheaper variant independently works. If losses grow, document complementarity instead.'),\n    ('g1-r0002-joint_count',\n     'Cross weighting type (target-aware/content/mean) with target-match slots (N,C,B,J versus N,0,0,0). New paired cells: mean_match versus mean_activity and content_match versus content_activity.',\n     'Existing attention pair g1-r0002-joint_count versus g1-r0003-attention_activity; same four-slot activity intervention and same-dimensional MLP in every cell.',\n     'Report both main effects and interaction on AUC and Logloss. If content beats mean by more than .0003 AUC conditional on matches but matches target-aware quality, prioritize generic learned weighting with direct relevance for repetition.',\n     'If mean/content gains over their activity controls are absent, counts may not transfer to these representation choices. Preserve the negative interaction result; choose the existing incumbent for assessment.'),\n]\nstudy = {\n    'id': 'g1-target-conditioning-after-direct-counts',\n    'protocol_ref': '9c1635366a72f4c4f67708ee7ae9b72a1b90197ffed3485736388ceff7c91d3e',\n    'evidence_refs': [\n        'baseline-static', 'baseline-pooled', 'baseline-din',\n        'g1-r0000-behavior_within', 'g1-r0000-interleaved_within',\n        'g1-r0000-behavior_global', 'g1-r0000-interleaved_global',\n        'g1-r0001-field_values', 'g1-r0001-collapsed_values', 'g1-r0001-collapsed_rms',\n        'g1-r0002-joint_count', 'g1-r0002-independent_count',\n        'g1-r0002-joint_rate', 'g1-r0002-independent_rate',\n        'g1-r0003-count_summary', 'g1-r0003-activity_summary', 'g1-r0003-attention_activity',\n    ],\n    'question': (\n        'After making direct target-match intensity explicit, is the complementary learned history signal supplied by trainable pooled values, '\n        'query-independent learned event importance, or target-conditioned weighting? Can a simpler same-width summary preserve quality at lower measured cost? '\n        'Observation: attention+matches g1-r0002-joint_count AUC .6171272214 exceeds count-only g1-r0003-count_summary .6130945529 '\n        'by .0040326685 and attention+activity g1-r0003-attention_activity .6132432588 by .0038839626. '\n        'The previous complete removal failed its quality objective; this discriminates which part should be retained.'\n    ),\n    'hypothesis': (\n        'Provisional mechanism: explicit bucket-match counts carry direct target relevance, while the remaining trainable history values carry '\n        'generic category/brand/action/recency composition. Counts may therefore reduce the incremental need for a target-conditioned scorer, '\n        'even though complete summary removal failed. Content-only weighting tests learned generic selection; uniform pooling additionally '\n        'removes learned selection. Counterevidence already exists: without counts, baseline-pooled AUC .6102261 is below baseline-din .6133620. '\n        'This is a new local controlled question about familiar mechanisms; no global architectural novelty is asserted.'\n    ),\n    'nearest_work': [\n        {\n            'source_ref': 'paper:din; arxiv:1706.06978v4; content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2; primary text lines 232-277',\n            'verification': 'read',\n            'difference': 'DIN discusses average/sum pooling, target-adaptive local activation and avoiding softmax to preserve intensity. Local reference uses normalized softmax and substituted category/brand/action/age fields. We retain explicit bounded count slots while replacing only the weighting query or the weighting operation. Neither pooling nor intensity preservation is claimed as new; no exact DIN reproduction.'\n        },\n        {\n            'source_ref': 'queryformer-paper-v1; arxiv:2609.16548v1; text-sha256:f8e114e22e2e8016610748784b98f2ffb59e5611f92ef03689e11f7aed4de3a6; primary section 5.2 Table 4, lines 224-249',\n            'verification': 'read',\n            'difference': 'Participant reports query-generation replacement and attention-removal losses in another task and split. Here test whether any direct target input to a shallow scorer is still necessary after explicit matches. No generated query, field bridge, packed views or source-recipe transfer; removal cannot isolate source query quality from capacity.'\n        },\n        {\n            'source_ref': 'unidot-paper-v1; arxiv:2608.16797v1; text-sha256:7714c79aba968b84d631bb677ca87a16614add7785fff830fd99b93e33b39727; primary section 5.3 Table 4, lines 683-731',\n            'verification': 'read',\n            'difference': 'Source tiny-mode cross-attention removal has a modest reported loss alongside pooled history. Local total summary removal lost .00403 AUC, so that simplification did not transfer. Test partial replacement by learned pooled values instead; no FM Highway, buses, extra supervision or optimizer change.'\n        },\n        {\n            'source_ref': 'trial://g1-r0002-joint_count; candidate.py initial SHA256 d16d? no: incumbent source is the exact current input recorded in the runtime history',\n            'verification': 'implementation_checked',\n            'difference': 'Inherit all embedding/scorer/output allocations and unchanged N,C,B,J calculations. Replace target-aware weights by uniform or zero-query learned weights, crossing each with exact N-only slot replacement from history_g1_r0003_attention_activity.py. Existing source and scores are the closest local reference, not a novelty comparator.'\n        },\n    ],\n    'inherited_components': [\n        'Frozen protocol, static benchmark attributes with undocumented as-of dates, causal supplied prefix, category/brand bucket semantics and missing-ID rules.',\n        'Parent additive 16-dimensional category, brand, action and logarithmic recency embeddings; shared static/history category and brand tables.',\n        'Parent scoring network Linear(4d,64), PReLU, Linear(64,1); all tensors created in original order, including dormant tensors.',\n        'Parent output MLP [128,64], static concatenation, a single d-dimensional history summary, and four normalized log-count channels.',\n        'N-only zero-slot control from g1-r0003-attention_activity; standard host optimizer, loss, labels and checkpointing.',\n    ],\n    'proposed_difference': (\n        'Four standalone modules implement a 3-by-2 design with two existing target-aware controls. '\n        'mean_match and mean_activity compute mask/N and never execute the scorer; trainable history values remain. '\n        'content_match and content_activity execute the unchanged scorer on [0,h,-h,0], removing target conditioning from weights '\n        'while keeping learned content selection. Prediction remains target dependent through static inputs, match slots when enabled, '\n        'and the final MLP. We do not claim a target-independent predictor or equal active capacity. '\n        'Earlier behavior slots (.611913 versus interleaved .613042) and separate field values (.613185 versus collapsed .613311) '\n        'did not justify finer learned partitions; count versus rate helped (~.00237 AUC), observed versus independent joint did not (~.000004). '\n        'Retain those unsuccessful directions and the failed total-removal hypothesis instead of restarting a tokenization claim. '\n        'The new difference is conditional replacement and the factorial contrast, not an invention of mean pooling.'\n    ),\n    'predictions': [\n        'Primary screening prediction: content_match is within .0003 absolute AUC of g1-r0002-joint_count and worsens Logloss by no more than .0001, while remaining above count-only g1-r0003-count_summary. Mean_match tests the stronger simplification with the same quality thresholds.',\n        'Partial-substitution prediction: (AUC_attention_activity - AUC_replacement_activity) minus (AUC_attention_match - AUC_replacement_match) is at least .0003 for each replacement; report the actual difference even if negative. This is a screening criterion, not a significance threshold.',\n        'If generic learned event importance is necessary, content_match exceeds mean_match by more than .0003 AUC; if not, mean pooling is sufficient within this implementation and protocol.',\n        'A cost-preserving mean candidate must reduce measured allocated GPU or train seconds by at least 5% at matched three passes while meeting both quality tolerances; wall time, peak memory, throughput and p50/p95 are reported separately. No content-mode speed claim is assumed.',\n        'Label-free first-512 diagnostics: mean/content summaries and weights stay invariant under within-field target rotation with histories fixed (RMS/L1 deltas <=1e-6), including empty histories. Mean nonempty effective event count equals N within numerical tolerance. These verify implementation, not predictive sufficiency.',\n        'Frozen host slice bins are exploratory: report counts, positives and negatives for all returned slices; inspect match-present/absent and history-length strata without selecting a winner on a slice. Small/single-class slices are insufficient, not evidence of no effect.',\n    ],\n    'falsifiers': [\n        'If both replacements lose more than .0003 AUC or .0001 Logloss against g1-r0002-joint_count, the proposed cheap-sufficiency prediction fails for these implementations. An AUC increase with a Logloss penalty is a tradeoff, not unconditional improvement.',\n        'If target-aware advantage does not shrink in the match condition relative to activity-only, explicit match counts have not substituted for target-dependent weighting as predicted.',\n        'If content-only weights do not outperform mean at useful quality/cost, learned generic event weighting is unsupported. If mean exceeds tolerances despite skipping the scorer, retire the learned-weighting necessity explanation locally.',\n        'Nonzero target-rotation summary dependence in mean/content mode, nonfinite outputs/diagnostics, shape errors, or broken masking invalidate an execution; retain charged failure receipts and repair before interpretation.',\n        'No >=5% measured training/GPU saving invalidates an efficiency claim even if prediction quality is retained. Unmeasured equal-compute quality and single-seed outcomes do not establish a frontier or repeated support.',\n    ],\n    'alternative_explanations': [\n        'The joint model may require a genuinely target-specific distributed history signal beyond exact bucket matches; the original pooling baseline and complete-removal failure support this competing explanation.',\n        'Removing the target query reduces effective input rank; changing event weights changes norm, gradient routing and conditioning. Allocated-parameter equality does not resolve these explanations. First-512 summary norms and concentration are only diagnostics.',\n        'Seed noise, checkpoint selection on reused validation and earlier branch selection may inflate small differences. All current comparisons are preliminary at seed 42; paired 42/43/44 validation repetitions and user-cluster intervals only if the host exposes authorized predictions are needed.',\n        '85.2% at the history limit in the earlier first-512 diagnostic is not a population estimate. Truncation, hash collisions and coarse vocabulary can make generic summaries appear sufficient; conclusions apply only to supplied prefixes, not full raw histories.',\n        'The static snapshot timing assumption remains unverified. This is benchmark modeling evidence rather than verified production point-in-time utility.',\n    ],\n    'contrasts': [dict(parent_ref=parent, intervention=intervention, control=control,\n                       held_fixed=fixed, remaining_confounds=confounds,\n                       decision_if_supported=yes, decision_if_not_supported=no)\n                  for parent, intervention, control, yes, no in contrast_specs],\n    'cost_plan': {\n        'estimate_ref': 'baseline-din wall 610.8195 s; baseline-pooled 578.9037 s; g1-r0002-joint_count 587.1395 s; g1-r0003-attention_activity 599.0447 s. Runtime full-unit estimate 704.3729729604 s, cap 1760.9324324011 s; remaining 76569.6625 s at resolution. Four proposed trials: ~2817.49 s at estimate, <=7043.73 s at cap. All preparation and host diagnostics charged; no training/calibration/installations in coding jail.',\n        'all_variants_counted': True,\n        'attribution_reserve': 'Reserve four additional full trial caps (~7043.73 s) for discriminating scale/effective-capacity replacements or a repaired promising branch, including failures. This is a reserve only, not authorization to execute unregistered variants. Current four cells are all counted; existing attention controls already paid. Stop speculation and reassess on receipts.',\n        'assessment_reserve': 'Reserve nine full trial caps (~15848.39 s) for one frozen final candidate plus the incumbent and the closest replacement control at paired seeds 42/43/44. Conservatively includes seed-42 reruns; accepted matching-hash receipts may be reused by host. Freeze exact source/config/checkpoint hashes, comparisons and commands before final validation assessment. No test feedback or closed archive is authorized.',\n        'stop_rule': 'Current suite plus attribution plus assessment reserves total ~29935.85 s at trial caps, below the resolved remaining budget before continued charged preparation. Admit follow-ups only when the refreshed ledger covers a complete unit plus reserves; never raise limits. Stop on hard cap, integrity failure, user stop or no admissible discriminating unit. This phase ends after proposal/source checks; host trains automatically. Do not wait for or launch training locally.',\n    },\n}\n# Record the exact parent source, avoiding an uncertain provenance locator.\nparent = Path('/workspace/history_g1_r0003_attention_activity.py').read_text()\nimport hashlib\nstudy['nearest_work'][-1]['source_ref'] = ('trial://g1-r0002-joint_count; incoming candidate source SHA256 '\n    + '7b779f8d1496047ef14988cfc814aaea' if False else\n    'trial://g1-r0002-joint_count; runtime receipt source_sha256 and candidate.py input; matched activity implementation history_g1_r0003_attention_activity.py SHA256 ' + hashlib.sha256(parent.encode()).hexdigest())\nassessments = [\n    {\n        'knowledge_id': 'taac2026-industry-2-unidot', 'decision': 'used',\n        'rationale': 'Reviewed the prior declared use against local removal outcomes and primary tiny-mode section 5.3. Source-motivated total attention removal did not preserve local quality (.617127 to .613095). That failed transfer motivates a narrower replacement retaining learned event values; it does not refute the source system.',\n        'transformed_mechanism': 'Replace target-conditioned attention by mean or content-only weighted learned values alongside inherited direct match counts, crossed with N-only controls.',\n        'variant_names': [v['name'] for v in variants],\n        'nearest_work_difference': 'No FM Highway, per-layer dots, buses, delay labels, source split or optimizer. Retains a shallow single summary; no global novelty or source-system reproduction.',\n        'falsifier': 'If replacements do not retain quality at measured benefit, local attention simplification remains unsupported. More source citation cannot override the negative result.'\n    },\n    {\n        'knowledge_id': 'taac2026-industry-1-queryformer', 'decision': 'used',\n        'rationale': 'Primary section 5.2 Table 4 reports query-related ablation losses in another setting. Use as competing evidence and a reason to test query necessity before expanding queries, not as evidence it transfers.',\n        'transformed_mechanism': 'Zero only the query input to the existing event scorer, crossed with explicit target-match counts and activity-only slots. Mean variants distinguish query removal from learned weighting removal.',\n        'variant_names': ['content_match', 'content_activity', 'mean_match', 'mean_activity'],\n        'nearest_work_difference': 'No generated probes, field bridge, packed multi-view execution or source training. Reduced active input rank remains a confound despite identical allocated scorer parameters.',\n        'falsifier': 'If content-only loses materially to target-aware weighting even with explicit matches, query-free sufficiency fails locally. This does not validate QueryFormer query generation.'\n    },\n    {\n        'knowledge_id': 'taac2026-academic-1-craft', 'decision': 'considered',\n        'rationale': 'Card reviewed; no local depth/transport instability diagnosed. Primary transport mechanism not audited in this turn.',\n        'transformed_mechanism': 'None; no transport gate or deep memory routing.', 'variant_names': [],\n        'nearest_work_difference': 'Single summary weighting substitution in a shallow model; source reliability-gated propagation is untested.',\n        'falsifier': 'Reconsider only after an admissible matched-depth diagnostic identifies propagation instability. This suite neither validates nor refutes the source mechanism.'\n    },\n    {\n        'knowledge_id': 'taac2026-academic-2-unidac', 'decision': 'considered',\n        'rationale': 'Organizer-level card only. Earlier action partition contrasts did not improve the reference; no old/recent complementary-utility contrast exists.',\n        'transformed_mechanism': 'None; no older-history compression, dual paths or gated exchange.', 'variant_names': [],\n        'nearest_work_difference': 'Same visible 128-event prefix and one summary; no domain interpretation of behavior types.',\n        'falsifier': 'Reconsider if controlled age/type marginal utility is observed. Uniform pooling is not a test of UniDAC.'\n    },\n    {\n        'knowledge_id': 'taac2026-academic-3-unitokenformer', 'decision': 'considered',\n        'rationale': 'Organizer-level card only; local field_values underperformed collapsed_values. This failed local finer-granularity branch is retained as evidence, not generalized to all tokenization.',\n        'transformed_mechanism': 'None; no learned token allocation or sequence decoder.', 'variant_names': [],\n        'nearest_work_difference': 'Changes weights within the existing summary width rather than allocating additional tokens.',\n        'falsifier': 'Revisit on controlled evidence of a field-specific bottleneck; this suite cannot refute the full source architecture.'\n    },\n]\nproposal = {'study': study, 'parent_trial': 'g1-r0002-joint_count', 'variants': variants,\n            'knowledge_assessments': assessments}\nPath('/workspace/proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\\\n')\nprint(json.dumps({'written': [v['file'] for v in variants] + ['proposal.json'], 'variant_names': [v['name'] for v in variants]}))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
